/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573268 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344566" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573268 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573268 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}}cos\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x))=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573268 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f397079-49a9-58d1-bc93-fa23602eefa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573268 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/86/86c0cf22de78e3b773543680c2ace077f97b66ae822436d637c5444903e2330f.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}}cos\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)) & =cos\\,(arctan\\,(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\  & =cos\\,(arctan\\,(\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573309 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573309 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152866" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573309 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573309 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573309 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1c19cde-3b7d-5f98-929b-d663820d03f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573309 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2}):$ \n\n![](images/ff/fffe2ba1124b8edd04902db5ad2b0945e5e04372ae0a0ed338c893f0ae417c58.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})$ is $x\\in [2,6].$ This means that $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})$ is undefined." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573339 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 1